# Arrow functions

Write TypeScript functions as arrows, including exports and helpers.

```typescript
export const fill = (text: string, tokens: FillTokens): string =>
  Mustache.render(text, tokens, undefined, {
    escape: (value) => String(value),
  });
```

Do not use `function` declarations (`function foo()` / `export async function foo()`). Methods on classes may stay method syntax.
